{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306133-mortal-sorcerers-in-the-realm","id":1306133,"title":"Mortal Sorcerers in the Realm","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-19T18:22:32-07:00","id":1306133,"title":"Mortal Sorcerers in the Realm","content":"So, I noticed that one of the rulers of House Nellens, Nellens Sabine, is a mortal sorcerer, and it got me thinking about the role that mortal sorcerers play in the Realm. I think that they could be divided into four primary groups. First, those who are scions of the Dynastic Houses or patrician families, who use their sorcery for the benefit of their Dynastic Houses or patrician families. Second, those who are mortal monks within the Immaculate Order, who use their sorcery to protect the spirit of the Realm. Third, those who are mortal specialists within the Imperial Legions, who use their sorcery to protect the security of the Realm. Fourth, those who are mortal bureaucrats of the Thousand Scales, who use their sorcery to protect the stability of the Realm.<br /> <br /> Now, how common are mortal sorcerers in the Realm? Probably more common than Dragon-Blooded sorcerers, maybe more common than Dragon-Blooded, but they are probably rare rather than merely uncommon. Basically, they are as common as an ST needs them to be.<br /> <br /> Regardless of how rare they are though, I doubt that the Scarlet Empress would have left much to chance, so I suggest the following system. Early in her reign, the Scarlet Empress created a semi-independent office within the Thousand Scales that was devoted to finding and testing mortal children with strange talents called the Guardians of Hidden Potential. When a potential sorcerer was discovered among the lower classes of the Realm, the office gave the parents an adequate payment for their mortal child, and the mortal child found themselves developing their potential within a dozen occult schools where they were indoctrinated into the service of the Realm. One-third of the schools were run by the Immaculate Order, one-third of the schools were run by the Imperial Legions, and one-third of the schools were run by the Thousand Scales. The mortal children of Dynastic Houses and patricians families were exempt from such recruitment, as their parents would have had sufficient resources to see to their training.<br /> <br /> The occult schools were fairly typical primary schools other than being devoted to developing mortal sorcery. Students who failed to develop sorcery ended up in the associated service as a monk, recruit, or bureaucrat, but they were monitored by their superiors to see if they blossomed into sorcery later in life. Students who did develop sorcery ended up in relative positions of prestige and power, in a place between mortals and Dragon-Blooded, using their talents for the benefit of the Realm and the Scarlet Empress. After twenty years of service to the Realm, they were allowed to chart their own fate, though the majority of them stayed in service to the Realm.<br /> <br /> Since the disappearance of the Scarlet Empress, the occult schools have been largely ignored by the Dynastic Houses, as they never had anything to do with them during the reign of the Scarlet Empress. The Scarlet Empress did not trust her descendants with control over mortal sorcerers, so she made sure that the office was controlled by mortal sorcerers who were loyal to her first, the Realm second, the service third, and the community of mortal sorcerers fourth. The Guardians of Hidden Potential have ruthlessly used its connections among the Immaculate Order, the Imperial Legions, and the Thousand Scales to protect the occult schools and to continue to serve the Realm in the best of their capabilities. While the Dynastic Houses are largely dismissive of the threat posed by mortal sorcerers, there are tens of thousands of them, and they could represent an important wild card any future civil war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25244-the-fool-of-creation","name":"The Fool of Creation","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T18:27:09-07:00","id":1306135,"title":"","content":"Mortal monks learn occult to combat spirits. They do not learn sorcery. Sorcery is uncommon and magic in general is treated with distrust in the realm. It is also impossible for a mortal to learn sorcery without the sorcery merit. Which is also a hard limitation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-19-2019, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T18:27:24-07:00","id":1306136,"title":"","content":"How does this ministry go about testing people?<br /> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306133-mortal-sorcerers-in-the-realm?p=1306135#post1306135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magic is uncommon and magic in general is treated with distrust in the realm.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span></div><br /> That doesn't matter. This is already a departure from the books from a person who has introduced themselves with a number of such things with a clear and common priority, so just... explore it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 04-19-2019, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T18:47:55-07:00","id":1306138,"title":"","content":"That is a good question. I imagine that there would be a number of tests involving games of chance, pattern recognition, strange drugs, etc. The Guardians of Hidden Potential would probably have a hundred different methodologies, though they would probably only bother testing children who were known oddities to their communities.<br /> <br /> As for learning Occult, I think that is impossible in 3e, as it seems to be an innate supernatural sensitivity. You are either born with the potential, have it invested in you through a process like Exaltation or Exigence, or you do without. I agree that Immaculate monks would probably claim that they were not doing sorcery, that they were merely receiving the blessings of the Immaculate Dragons through the piety of their prayers, and their method of initiation and their merits would reflect such a philosophy, but their effects would mechanically be identical to sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25244,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25244-the-fool-of-creation","user":"The Fool of Creation","date":". 04-19-2019, 09:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25244-the-fool-of-creation","name":"The Fool of Creation","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T19:03:47-07:00","id":1306141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Fool of Creation</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306133-mortal-sorcerers-in-the-realm?p=1306138#post1306138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is a good question. I imagine that there would be a number of tests involving games of chance, pattern recognition, strange drugs, etc. The Guardians of Hidden Potential would probably have a hundred different methodologies, though they would probably only bother testing children who were known oddities to their communities.<br /> <br /> As for learning Occult, I think that is impossible in 3e, as it seems to be an innate supernatural sensitivity. You are either born with the potential, have it invested in you through a process like Exaltation or Exigence, or you do without. I agree that Immaculate monks would probably claim that they were not doing sorcery, that they were merely receiving the blessings of the Immaculate Dragons through the piety of their prayers, and their method of initiation and their merits would reflect such a philosophy, but their effects would mechanically be identical to sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Learning occult and actually practicing sorcery are completely two different things and you can learn occult and be an exorcist without being a sorcerer. In fact, sorcery doesn't really have a way to banish spirits if I remember currently. Regardless having everyone use sorcereres kind of causes it's mysticism to go away and you can't do something that's similar but equal. Regardless of how you learn it. Sorcery is Sorcery is Sorcery. There's no way around it in this edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T19:34:32-07:00","id":1306145,"title":"","content":"Exorcism is a form of thaumaturgy, and mortal thaumaturgy is exceedingly rare (Exalted 3e, p. 490). The most common form of mortal thaumaturgy is tea ceremony, which is 1:10,000 in regions that drink tea. Thaumaturgy can hardly be considered common enough to account for all of the mortal magic in Creation, which is why I suggest that mortal sorcerers are more common than mortal thaumaturges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25244-the-fool-of-creation","name":"The Fool of Creation","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T19:37:45-07:00","id":1306147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Fool of Creation</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306133-mortal-sorcerers-in-the-realm?p=1306145#post1306145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exorcism is a form of thaumaturgy, and mortal thaumaturgy is exceedingly rare (Exalted 3e, p. 490). The most common form of mortal thaumaturgy is tea ceremony, which is 1:10,000 in regions that drink tea. Thaumaturgy can hardly be considered common enough to account for all of the mortal magic in Creation, which is why I suggest that mortal sorcerers are more common than mortal thaumaturges.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mortal sorcerery is even more uncommon than that of thaumaturgy though. Unless you plan on completely changing the setting, sorcery in the realm for dragon blooded is limited to one school. Until the Realm comes out we might not know what the numbers of mortal sorcerers are in the realm but one would guess it's probably low maybe enough to get one or two schools going but with the immaculate philosophy, mortals learning sorcery would probably be an even bigger issue.<br /> <br /> The immaculate philosophy is actually all based on a strict hierarchy. In first edition, at least, everything about the hierarchy was set in place. You had a place in life and you couldn't move up or down it. Beings such as farmers owe the dragon blooded and honor him by paying taxes just as livestock owed it's life to to the farmer. Now at the same time the dragon blooded still had to be respectful to the farmer and the farmer respectful to the livestock. Disruptions to this hierarchy is basically the same as breaking the ten commandments. That they happen in an imperfect world is of course the subject of philosophical debate but as the religion of the realm it is of very defining importance.<br /> <br /> The point is, that mortal sorcerers are a huge gray spot. It's not hard to see them as attempting to move above their station. I could see a lot of other locations that don't practice the the immaculate philosophy to have a number of sorcerers but it's hard to see the realm as it is. At least openly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-19-2019, 11:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T20:00:32-07:00","id":1306153,"title":"","content":"Sorcery among mortals is more rare than thaumaturgy. Yes, you have to be born with the potential for the latter, but it's still more common occurrence than a mortal who has the right stuff discovering that he has the potential to shape the mystical forces underpinning reality, and successfully awakening himself into that strange world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T23:20:22-07:00","id":1306183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Fool of Creation</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306133-mortal-sorcerers-in-the-realm?p=1306145#post1306145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exorcism is a form of thaumaturgy, and mortal thaumaturgy is exceedingly rare (Exalted 3e, p. 490). The most common form of mortal thaumaturgy is tea ceremony, which is 1:10,000 in regions that drink tea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tea reading is &quot;at least one&quot; per ten thousand, not an average of one per ten thousand. Further, this leaves unspecified the ratio of tea readers to other thaumaturges in tea-drinking regions, and thus entirely fails to tell us the overall rate of thaumaturgy Creation-wide. If we reasonably expect an average of three tea readers per ten thousand in places where tea is important, and four other kinds of thaumaturges (divided among lower-frequency gifts) per tea reader, we get a rate of fifteen thaumaturges per ten thousand population, or one per 667 mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T01:08:27-07:00","id":1306197,"title":"","content":"Also if the Imperial City was the size of the ancient city of Rome, that\u2019s still be 100 legit tea leaf readers spread throughout the city there. Since Exalted is a fantasy world I wouldn\u2019t even be surprised if the Imperial City was double that. Or at least has a higher concentration of thaumaturges working there in the big smoke.<br /> <br /> So if we have like 200-250 tea leaf readers alone, then we could still have like 20-30 mortal sorcerers and say \u201cfor every ten tea leaf reader there is one who got far beyond, a true sorcerer.\u201d<br /> <br /> I also think it\u2019s a bit silly to have a ton mortal sorcerers around anyway. They still have the power to part seas and summon thunderstorms. Terrestrial sorcerers are EPIC. Plus with how many exorcists and hedge witches and stuff that the setting requires having that many more mortal sorcs is just a lot.<br /> <br /> THAT being said, would Big Red want to capitalize on that? Absolutely! They\u2019re mortals so they\u2019re easier to control than dynasty, and they can friggin turn a severe storm into a straight up hurricane! So a school for them is not out of the question whatsoever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 04-20-2019, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T03:01:46-07:00","id":1306208,"title":"","content":"This approach creates a power bloc of empowered peasants and indoctrination doesn't stop that from being a problem, it arguably makes it worse.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T09:32:29-07:00","id":1306266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306133-mortal-sorcerers-in-the-realm?p=1306183#post1306183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tea reading is &quot;at least one&quot; per ten thousand, not an average of one per ten thousand. Further, this leaves unspecified the ratio of tea readers to other thaumaturges in tea-drinking regions, and thus entirely fails to tell us the overall rate of thaumaturgy Creation-wide. If we reasonably expect an average of three tea readers per ten thousand in places where tea is important, and four other kinds of thaumaturges (divided among lower-frequency gifts) per tea reader, we get a rate of fifteen thaumaturges per ten thousand population, or one per 667 mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue is how many of these tea-readers do anything besides occassioanl read tea. Or how many can do it and never try. It's notable as bit that this points tea-readers are rarer than identical twins on a couple order of magnitude. I would assume the subset <i>of them</i> who even do anything with it or more so is less so.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is a bit of an example of how giving numbers to things like this leads to brain spiders &lt;_&lt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T10:19:39-07:00","id":1306276,"title":"","content":"How much is the &quot;rate&quot; of sorcerers affected by the Realm doing lots of suppressing things towards magic being understood and practiced by mortals? It makes sense that they would manage and co-opt those that they do come across, but that number may be less than elsewhere.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm fully down with a version of the Realm where they have lots of &quot;Imperial Wizards&quot; of a sort about, used in the service of military campaigns, industry etc. with lots of control at a high political level, prohibitions against too much fraternization, etc.<br /> <br /> (Not least because it makes the destiny of the Sorcerer more useful for Sidereals).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T10:35:10-07:00","id":1306280,"title":"","content":"Unless the Realm book says otherwise, I'll probably go with with the following: mortal sorcerers in the Realm are overwhelmingly dynasts by birth, and every single one of those went through the Heptagram. A few patrician sorcerers are allowed to practice sorcery with permission from the Empress. Some of these are directly overseen by a bureau of the Ten Thousand Scales, while others are allowed to pursue their own careers.<br /> <br /> Mortal sorcerers who don't fit into these categories are dealt with extremely harshly (despite persistent rumors that the All-Seeing-Eye employs at least a few)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":541,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","user":"LeTipex","date":". 04-20-2019, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T12:52:25-07:00","id":1306309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306133-mortal-sorcerers-in-the-realm?p=1306197#post1306197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if we have like 200-250 tea leaf readers alone, then we could still have like 20-30 mortal sorcerers and say \u201cfor every ten tea leaf reader there is one who got far beyond, a true sorcerer.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to note here that there's no indication that thaumaturgy and sorcery are correlated among mortals. While Exalts who get Terrestrial Circle Sorcery become thaumaturges for free, mortals do not.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T12:56:42-07:00","id":1306311,"title":"","content":"I'd go similar with LeTipix. There are mortal sorcerers in the Realm, but they often were from backgrounds of privelege and luxury to do so, or were individuals with enough weight as sorcerers to be recruited. The Realm doesn't mass-produce them since it well, can't. The handful of known sorcerers in the Realm are notable <i>because they're sorcerers</i>. So it's not like there's this imperial service that has sorcerers specially trained and has procedures. It's a range of very unique, powerful, and valuable individuals the Realm has drawn from folks who might be allowed to do so and doesn't consdier a threat. There's no like, department they work in or standard use in the Imperial government. Instead, they're indivdiuals who probably got to particualr notable places of power in the Great Houses or Thousand Scales in part because being a sorcerer gives you a leg-up, but also puts you in a position that siding wiht the power is better than being against it.<br /> <br /> Unaccounted for sorcerers probably operate underground, doing weird personal projects and all that. A good example of this is Bomanz in the Black Company series. He was a sorcerer who as it turns out more or less did his stuff under the radar, had his big project he was working on and eventually it exploded and released the Lady and Ten Who Were Taken. I think he's a good illustration of what non-registered sorcerers in the Realm are like, as well as the sort of reason the Realm likes to keep a clamp down on unaccounted sorcerers in general.<br /> <br /> Remember that in general, with a few workings, sorcerers techncially don't count as &quot;mortal&quot; save in an academic sense. Sorcery does a lot ot open up individual power, but it also allow syou to break a lot of the norms of the Realm, a society very much built on enforcing those norms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T14:29:11-07:00","id":1306337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306133-mortal-sorcerers-in-the-realm?p=1306309#post1306309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to note here that there's no indication that thaumaturgy and sorcery are correlated among mortals. While Exalts who get Terrestrial Circle Sorcery become thaumaturges for free, mortals do not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeeeah I thought about that while I was writing that sentence. I was more looking at it from the perspective of a random creationite who just sees magic people as magic people and doesn\u2019t understand that thaunaturges and sorcerers aren\u2019t really related. Like if he\u2019s from a village that worships an elemental as a god he might not appreciate the difference when you insist that gods and elementals are completely different things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T19:50:18-07:00","id":1306396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306133-mortal-sorcerers-in-the-realm?p=1306309#post1306309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to note here that there's no indication that thaumaturgy and sorcery are correlated among mortals. While Exalts who get Terrestrial Circle Sorcery become thaumaturges for free, mortals do not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, that is only true for Solars. Dragonblooded and Lunars do <b>not </b>get Thaumaturgy bundled in with their Terrestrial Circle Sorcery.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T21:16:59-07:00","id":1306422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306133-mortal-sorcerers-in-the-realm?p=1306396#post1306396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, that is only true for Solars. Dragonblooded and Lunars do <b>not </b>get Thaumaturgy bundled in with their Terrestrial Circle Sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, <i>actually</i>-actually, all Exalted get the Merit when they become sorcerers.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted Core Rules, p.166</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted characters who take the Charm Terrestrial Circle Sorcery (see pgs. 360-361) gain this Merit [Thaumaturgist] at no cost.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted Core Rules, p.490</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When one of the Chosen unlocks the power of sorcery, she gains this Merit [Thaumaturgist] automatically.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted Core Rules, p.25</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Chosen:</b> <i>See Exalted.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>And there is nothing in either the Dragon-Blooded book, nor the released-to-backers Lunars draft, to contradict that.<br /> <br /> I do not know how you came by the misimpression that Exalted other than Solars do not gain the Thaumaturgist Merit for free when they become sorcerers, but you did not get it from the actual game books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T00:02:26-07:00","id":1306455,"title":"","content":"Presumably they forgot that bit was in the merit and not the solar sorcery charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T02:29:41-07:00","id":1306480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306133-mortal-sorcerers-in-the-realm?p=1306422#post1306422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not know how you came by the misimpression that Exalted other than Solars do not gain the Thaumaturgist Merit for free when they become sorcerers, but you did not get it from the actual game books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it was not mentioned in their charms.<br /> <br /> ... and it is not mentioned in the Solar charm either, so, <i>okay</i>. Thank you for the correction.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T04:51:49-07:00","id":1306505,"title":"","content":"On Blaque and LeTipex's comments, I think maybe this certainly comes down to your taste about playing out and emphasizing the Realm as governed by oppressive norms through the Immaculate Philosophy vs the stance that the Immaculate Philosophy is actually shaped by the Sidereals for the Realm's hegemonic advantage and to support the society that they find safest and most amenable to control, and that they have latitude to manipulate &quot;purity&quot; status within its hierachy to serve their ends.<br /> <br /> (Certainly, I think, either stance taken, definitely include consideration the latter - if we don't, we maybe get the things like the Sidereals writing themselves into the Immaculate Philosophy as anathema from 1e which didn't really make the most sense!)<br /> <br /> That is - Is this the sort of thing that your vision of the Realm+Bronze alliance is going to co-opt and subordinate, without detracting from its oppressive character, or suppress totally as a threat? In my vision, the Realm+Bronze would tend to only suppress totally as a threat the declared Anathema and threats from outside Creation (fae, dead, demons), with a lot more latitude to coopt with accommodations much else (co-opting, without actively cultivating). Within this framework, I wouldn't tend to view scattered mortal sorcerers as much of a threat to the Realm+bronze and totally the sort of thing that they wouldn't worry too much about and would co-opt, and not in any case as saying too much about how oppressive for mortals the IP is (a few scattered mortals winning the lottery of the potential for sorcery attaining the heights doesn't say much at all about the general condition of Realm society!). This totally depends on your vision of the Realm, though, which has some space to vary.<br /> <br /> I agree about Blaque's thing on there being likely no sorcery &quot;department&quot; as I'd tend to envision it, and that they'd be more likely to be consulting adjuncts with some institutional relationship to the Heptagram and the formal institutions of the Realm. But if you were considering that, caveat with considering that a lot of historical bureaucracies and ministries before the modern 19th-20th century era of pretty large governments still existed without tending to have many employees (the kind of bureaucracy that you had in medieval China / Raj India etc was often pretty fairly minimal in terms of actual headcount), so rarity of mortal sorcerers is not quite a total argument against it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T07:45:46-07:00","id":1306524,"title":"","content":"A lot of it to me is less actually the Bronze Faction and more the Empress. She liked having a lot of control of the reigns of power, and some dumbass doing a big sorcery project ot summon a big demon or rewrite the leylines in an area is something she would rather not have to spend resrouces dealing with the cosnequences of. My views on the Realm trying to co-opt sorcerers to serve it when possible is purely power-play, with the societal norms being part of that. I tend to see the Bronze Faction as while an important cabal, still a cabal trying to affect a giant nation with complex insittutions that look more like the British Empire at times than some of the clasical ones the Realm draws on (it's navy does as well). The Realm is pretty enormous and well-run, which indicates at least a fairly intricate bureacracy and has been described as such in the books for the game's lifetime.<br /> <br /> Mind, this goes wiht my general view that states are greater than one person and the Realm having a super-strong central power base doesn't preclude having to have institutions devleoped to extend that beyond direct control. The norms of the Philosophy plus the complicated checks and systems fo the bureaucracy serve this, but indivdiual sorcercers can be disruptive, regardless of what they do. Mortals doing it probably are at risk of becoming Anathema or causing issues in general by getting too big for their britches. Folks who break the norms of a regulated society often hve to be made to fit in the society. Those that don't well, go underground. There's good story to be had by those ones, which is why I think it's soemthing I would emphasize wiht mortal sorcerers in the Realm who choose not to become part of the government in some fashion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T07:53:02-07:00","id":1306526,"title":"","content":"To expand on my indoctrination comment.<br /> <br /> Indoctrination makes people loyal to the image you've cultivated, the person you want to be which reality often falls short of, especially when your will is experienced through institutions under your control. So a peasant-born mortal sorcerer might condemn an uprising as a perversion of the natural order or they might participate in it because they see injustice done in the name of the Scarlet Empress by corrupt officials.<br /> <br /> People often misuse indoctrination when they\u2019re world building in order to hand-wave the possibility of a group or individual using their power in a way that\u2019s not in line with the greater good. The idea that indoctrination produces effective results bug gosh darn it we love freedom too much is one of those insidious pro-authoritarian myths that\u2019s perpetuated through fiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T08:08:14-07:00","id":1306528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306133-mortal-sorcerers-in-the-realm?p=1306526#post1306526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...not in line with the greater good.</div> </div> </div> </div>The greater good...<br /> <br /> \u200bOkay, ow, sorry.<br /> <br /> I expect that as others have indicated, most of the opportunity to <i>realize</i> any latent sorcerous potential, is going to generally occur in the Dynasty. And while it's a smaller group, the way the Realm generally treats sorcery leaves them likelier to notice that potential in young Dynasts than might occur in the Threshold, so while the number of sorcerers in the Realm is smaller than it <i>could</i> be, it's still probably greater than it is in the Threshold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-21-2019, 11:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T05:13:40-07:00","id":1306802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306133-mortal-sorcerers-in-the-realm?p=1306524#post1306524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of it to me is less actually the Bronze Faction and more the Empress. She liked having a lot of control of the reigns of power, and some dumbass doing a big sorcery project ot summon a big demon or rewrite the leylines in an area is something she would rather not have to spend resrouces dealing with the cosnequences of.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense as an argument. I'd not follow it and I'd tend to see the Empress as less interested in constraining the amount of plates that are spinning than utilizing them for her personal power and the power of the Realm, and really possibly mortals using sorcery potentially as another independent resource she can draw on or use independently of the Houses (and probably another loosely monitored factor now she has disappeared). The gain of utility is higher than the costs of odd sorcerous things happening.<br /> <br /> I was more aiming at the idea that suppression of mortal sorcerers is an inevitable consequence of the playing out of the Immaculate Philosophy's hierarchical propositions, but if that's not your argument....<br /> <br /> On a tangent to this topic, I was wondering if anyone else was considering attitudes might change with type of sorcerous initiation (some are more profane and bespeak more compromised loyalties than others), or if that's not a valid factor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T06:18:07-07:00","id":1306820,"title":"","content":"One of my main arguments against an administrative organ dedicated specifically to assessing the sorcerous potential of the general population would be that even if the Realm possessed the resources to set up such an apparatus comprehensively, it would be supremely inefficient; the costs of it would likely be huge, and the returns very small in comparison. It feels a lot like building an oil rig in order to tap about $1000 worth of crude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T08:41:37-07:00","id":1306859,"title":"","content":"Hmm.... The OP is really talking about (and I quote) &quot;<i>a semi-independent office within the Thousand Scales that was devoted to finding and testing mortal children with strange talents</i>&quot;, so I'd presume even within his/her paradigm, it's not like &quot;Here's the magical SAT, for all&quot;, rather something like an office that' s generally scanning around for occult potential and strange occult phenomena (the X-Files of the Realm or what have you) and then descends periodically to assess whether there's anything of the sort actually about beyond rumor. Intelligence led operations, essentially.<br /> <br /> (Although if we are talking about general assessment, I think that while there's that, there's also the question of whether there even is or should be ability to systematically assess potential, in setting. It seems like the non- or fuzzy predictability of sorcerers, even to the characters who should be best at it, the Sidereals, is fairly useful for the setting?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T09:41:49-07:00","id":1306868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306133-mortal-sorcerers-in-the-realm?p=1306859#post1306859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm.... The OP is really talking about (and I quote) &quot;<i>a semi-independent office within the Thousand Scales that was devoted to finding and testing mortal children with strange talents</i>&quot;, so I'd presume even within his/her paradigm, it's not like &quot;Here's the magical SAT, for all&quot;, rather something like an office that' s generally scanning around for occult potential and strange occult phenomena (the X-Files of the Realm or what have you) and then descends periodically to assess whether there's anything of the sort actually about beyond rumor. Intelligence led operations, essentially.<br /> <br /> (Although if we are talking about general assessment, I think that while there's that, there's also the question of whether there even is or should be ability to systematically assess potential, in setting. It seems like the non- or fuzzy predictability of sorcerers, even to the characters who should be best at it, the Sidereals, is fairly useful for the setting?)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the big thing in 3e is that the potential for being a sorcerer is still pretty rare, different from person to person, and so on. There's probably just not enough sorcerers, and how each srocerer goes about being a sorcerer is different enough for mortals or the self-trained that there need not be such a system. If a mortal wants to learn it with government or sanctioned society a way, there's the Heptagram. If they learned it on their own, they probably are given some job in a house or in the Thousand Scales fitting their expertise. And if not the above, they fit into the &quot;Forbidden hidden mage&quot; trope that is pretty common in media and fits them.<br /> <br /> I think a less fuzzy predictor is actually <i>not</i> helpful for the setting. The diea that mortal sorcerers are exotic enough that they are taken as individuals I think helps reinforce the general implications of exotic sorcery has this edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T09:50:40-07:00","id":1306874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306133-mortal-sorcerers-in-the-realm?p=1306859#post1306859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">something like an office that' s generally scanning around for occult potential and strange occult phenomena (the X-Files of the Realm or what have you) and then descends periodically to assess whether there's anything of the sort actually about beyond rumor.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though that's something that would technically cost less, but the ratio between costs and productive returns would be even worse.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T10:28:26-07:00","id":1306891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306133-mortal-sorcerers-in-the-realm?p=1306874#post1306874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel as though that's something that would technically cost less, but the ratio between costs and productive returns would be even worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could be! Seems harder to assess - a lot more dependent on assumptions how much sort of magical infrastructure you could set up to assist managing that sort of thing, how much your predictive magic helps with that sort of thing, how much of this you're having to do anyway as part of the Realm's internal security (against anathema, peasant revolts, Fair Folk intrusion and so on etc.). Whereas the big bureaucracy doing standardized tests on everyone for magical potential is pretty bad in upfront cost and return under any set of assumptions. It's not exactly my idea either way though, just trying to get back to what OP seems to be talking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T11:13:37-07:00","id":1306909,"title":"","content":"Un-Exalted sorcerers are much, much rarer than thaumaturgists. The numbers are not comparable.<br /> <br /> In the Realm, the Great Houses and patrician families generally attempt to direct the sorcerous potential of un-Exalted family members toward their own ends (or dedicate such children to the Immaculate Order). Immaculate monks keep an eye out for signs of sorcerous or thaumaturgic talent among the peasantry; the Order tries to induct such potentials as monks or draw them into its orbit as lay assets, where their inauspicious powers can be directed toward righteous ends. This is touched on only tangentially in <i>The Realm</i>; hopefully we'll get a chance to address it at greater length in <i>Paths of Brigid</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T12:11:23-07:00","id":1306931,"title":"","content":"Why would the Immaculate Faith treat mortal sorcery as anything other than the direst violation of the natural order?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/587-kukla","name":"Kukla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T12:15:43-07:00","id":1306934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306133-mortal-sorcerers-in-the-realm?p=1306931#post1306931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would the Immaculate Faith treat mortal sorcery as anything other than the direst violation of the natural order?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it's not the <i>direst</i> violation, and because even those possessed of inauspicious power can often still find a place to serve the Perfected Hierarchy (see also: Exigents, God-Blooded, thaumaturgists, etc.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T12:19:23-07:00","id":1306937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306133-mortal-sorcerers-in-the-realm?p=1306859#post1306859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm.... The OP is really talking about\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>The OP is talking about the Realm having more mortal sorcerers than it has thaumaturges, more mortal sorcerers than it has <i>Dragon-Blooded at all</i>. <br /> <br /> If it turns out this guy <i>wasn't</i> a sock-puppet for Aya Tari to circumvent his ban, I'll be very surprised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T12:21:41-07:00","id":1306938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306133-mortal-sorcerers-in-the-realm?p=1306934#post1306934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it's not the <i>direst</i> violation, and because even those possessed of inauspicious power can often still find a place to serve the Perfected Hierarchy (see also: Exigents, God-Blooded, thaumaturgists, etc.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems like a pretty big departure from the first edition which had the IO be against it due to the perfected hierarchy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T12:22:30-07:00","id":1306940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306133-mortal-sorcerers-in-the-realm?p=1306937#post1306937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The OP is talking about the Realm having more mortal sorcerers than it has thaumaturges, more mortal sorcerers than it has <i>Dragon-Blooded at all</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, that's as maybe but in the context of responding to Isator post that would've all been pretty irrelevant for me to note?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T12:22:47-07:00","id":1306941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306133-mortal-sorcerers-in-the-realm?p=1306931#post1306931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would the Immaculate Faith treat mortal sorcery as anything other than the direst violation of the natural order?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Order is parsimonious in such condemnations; it typically allows the wielders of inauspicious power \u2014 whether un-Exalted sorcerers, God-Blooded, Exigents, or the like \u2014 the opportunity to deploy that power under Immaculate supervision toward righteous ends, the better to expunge its stain in future incarnations. More specifically, sorcerers and thaumaturgists are most valued in the Order as seers, whose divinations contribute to the Wyld Hunt's ability to discover newly fledged Anathema.<br /> <br /> (This also provides plausible deniability for Sidereal divination, which can be attributed to the work of the Order's divinatory corps.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T12:24:45-07:00","id":1306942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306133-mortal-sorcerers-in-the-realm?p=1306938#post1306938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems like a pretty big departure from the first edition which had the IO be against it due to the perfected hierarchy.</div> </div> </div> </div>1e had mortal sorcerers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T12:27:04-07:00","id":1306943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306133-mortal-sorcerers-in-the-realm?p=1306942#post1306942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1e had mortal sorcerers?</div> </div> </div> </div>It had mortals. Who could enlighten their essence and become sorcerers. However, in general the IO frowned on sorcery more than other places. When I last read it anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T12:43:42-07:00","id":1306948,"title":"","content":"Being a thing observed by the Immaculate Order does strike me as both an application of their remit as the guardians of public morality and something that could be effectively delegated from state management in a manner that saves on overhead while belonging to a body regarded as loyal and trustworthy. In that, it would be reminiscent of the roles that established religious and monastic organisations have often played.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306133-mortal-sorcerers-in-the-realm?p=1306938#post1306938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That seems like a pretty big departure from the first edition which had the IO be against it due to the perfected hierarchy.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bThat sounds like an accurate description, yes.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306133-mortal-sorcerers-in-the-realm?p=1306941#post1306941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Order is parsimonious in such condemnations; it typically allows the wielders of inauspicious power \u2014 whether un-Exalted sorcerers, God-Blooded, Exigents, or the like \u2014 the opportunity to deploy that power under Immaculate supervision toward righteous ends, the better to expunge its stain in future incarnations. More specifically, sorcerers and thaumaturgists are most valued in the Order as seers, whose divinations contribute to the Wyld Hunt's ability to discover newly fledged Anathema.<br /> <br /> (This also provides plausible deniability for Sidereal divination, which can be attributed to the work of the Order's divinatory corps.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there something to be said for cases in which sorcerous initiation is, if not accidental, intuitive in a manner that doesn't speak to having deliberately sought such power out in defiance of one's appointed place","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T15:10:45-07:00","id":1306997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306133-mortal-sorcerers-in-the-realm?p=1306943#post1306943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It had mortals. Who could enlighten their essence and become sorcerers.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Enlighted Mortals were introduced in the Player's Guide but there's nothing there saying they had access to Sorcery and I distinctly remember people taking note of how White and Black Treatise made mortal sorcerers a part of the setting. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T15:14:56-07:00",