ade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T15:38:19-07:00","id":1307013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306133-mortal-sorcerers-in-the-realm?p=1307006#post1307006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do not believe that Terrestrial Circle Sorcery has any such potential.</div> </div> </div> </div>Death of Obsidian butterflies is not at the scale of rain of doom but it's still a small scale nuke that can pretty easily kill battlegroups and severally injure dragon blooded if they aren't prepared for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T16:05:12-07:00","id":1307025,"title":"","content":"*big dragon blinking all five eyes in quiet surprise*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/587-kukla","name":"Kukla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T16:08:24-07:00","id":1307026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Apromor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306133-mortal-sorcerers-in-the-realm?p=1307005#post1307005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bagrash Kol (sp?) was a mortal sorcerer who created an empire using the eye of autochthon in 1rst edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kol was always just a Scav Lord who came across the Eye I think? Like how The Perfect wasn't really a sorcerer or anything before discovering the staff.<br /> <br /> Epimethius and Lioness thanks for the clarifications; I had thought they weren't about - certainly the conversation didn't talk as if they had any importance, and kind of fits better with my recollection to be a 2e Enlightened Mortals thing (but I can't really remember 100%).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T16:10:48-07:00","id":1307028,"title":"","content":"Religions and large organizations in the real world aren't really known for lack of internal contradictions, nor for laser-focused adherence to a shortlist of enumerated core principles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T16:21:40-07:00","id":1307032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306133-mortal-sorcerers-in-the-realm?p=1307013#post1307013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Death of Obsidian butterflies is not at the scale of rain of doom but it's still a small scale nuke that can pretty easily kill battlegroups and severally injure dragon blooded if they aren't prepared for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So a principle that regular people shouldn't be allowed to possess nukes also means they shouldn't be allowed to own gasoline?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T16:24:21-07:00","id":1307034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306133-mortal-sorcerers-in-the-realm?p=1307032#post1307032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So a principle that regular people shouldn't be allowed to possess nukes also means they shouldn't be allowed to own gasoline?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean if they can use it to do bad things to beings who are considered their spiritual superior. Yes. That's what the perfected hierarchy advocates. I'm glad we're getting somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T16:27:42-07:00","id":1307037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306133-mortal-sorcerers-in-the-realm?p=1307034#post1307034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean if they can use it to do bad things to beings who are considered their spiritual superior. Yes. That's what the perfected hierarchy advocates.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about a unit of archers? Is that bad because people can use it to kill large numbers and a surprised Exalt? <br /> <br /> Keeping in mind that actual possession of arms is going to be regulated by the authorities?<br /> <br /> As sorcery is being presented as being? Because let's not lose sight of the fact that the Immaculate Order is stated to find it justifiable for some people to be initiated into sorcery when they do so under the supervision and guidance of the Immaculate Order. Leaving that detail out to shift the narrative in a direction implying that somebody is suggesting that the Order is advocating an egalitarian position is disingenuous.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T16:32:07-07:00","id":1307039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306133-mortal-sorcerers-in-the-realm?p=1307037#post1307037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about a unit of archers? Is that bad because people can use it to kill large numbers and a surprised Exalt?<br /> <br /> Keeping in mind that actual possession of arms is going to be regulated by the authorities?<br /> <br /> As sorcery is being presented as being? Because let's not lose sight of the fact that the Immaculate Order is stated to find it justifiable for some people to be initiated into sorcery when they do so under the supervision and guidance of the Immaculate Order. Leaving that detail out to shift the narrative in a direction implying that somebody is suggesting that the Order is advocating an egalitarian position is disingenuous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on if they use it against exalts or not. However, sorcery is already frowned upon in general. Arming mortals with magic is completely different than a weapon and much harder to control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T16:45:24-07:00","id":1307047,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306133-mortal-sorcerers-in-the-realm?p=1307039#post1307039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Depends on if they use it against exalts or not.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Hence the organisation into armies or being under monk supervision.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">However, sorcery is already frowned upon in general.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Sorcery is considered weird and creepy and makes one a bit of a pariah. There's still a whole school for it.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Arming mortals with magic</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bIs a misreading of the proposed scenario at best; the developers have not said that the Order is actively developing sorcerers, but that they keep an eye out for those who are already showing signs of it.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">is completely different than a weapon and much harder to control. </span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How much harder to control? They can't learn spells without texts and tutors. The kinds of workings they can perform in the first place have limited scope, and workings take weeks to accomplish; it's not hard to think of ways in which people could be regulated to make it hard for them to devote their attention to it. They're being watched by the Exalted, including powerful warriors who can likely put them down without much trouble if they stray too far.<br /> <br /> And of course, there are the benefits of the soft power approach; positive reinforcement and material benefits. Being a monk might not be as good as you could get striking out on your own, but it's more than you had on your own and has the benefit of being socially acceptable and resonating with your pre-existing values, which most examples are liable to want to stick to.<br /> <br /> Sorcery is not like being Celestial Exalted, it doesn't present so severe a threat that a 1% chance of a sorcerer effectively going rogue has to be treated like an absolute certainty.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T17:02:53-07:00","id":1307054,"title":"","content":"There's a question of what the alternative thing to do with the occasional peasant sorcerer is.<br /> <br /> For one thing, it's not as if leniency is going to encourage it to a point where it could threaten the stability of the Realm; sorcerous potential is still quite unlikely, you could give most of those people free access to the libraries of the Heptagram and it would do them no good.<br /> <br /> And it's not the Warhammer Imperium; they're not psykers who have a distressingly high chance of experiencing severe mental instability, becoming conduits for malefic entities or wielding power that might go out of control and make them explode, and the Realm has more varied attitudes than kill on sight for anything that isn't a Solar or Lunar.<br /> <br /> So presuming an inadvertent sorcerer who has not yet done anything conventionally criminal, what are the other options?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T18:00:01-07:00","id":1307081,"title":"","content":"Given who controls the levers of wealth on the Blessed Isle, the practical careers for a basely-born sorcerer on the Blessed Isle are Immaculate monk, employee of the Imperial Government, retainer of a Great House, or revolutionary living in hiding. Forcing them all to become the last by refusing to co-opt them into society via at least one of the other three would be just plain stupid.<br /> <br /> I guess if the Immaculate Order was entirely composed of excessively-devout persons with no care at all for worldly power, they might refuse to try to recruit them. But it would be a quite implausible state religion if that were true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T20:54:02-07:00","id":1307125,"title":"","content":"I guess that makes sense! I suppose I'm mostly thinking about the process by which a mortal _becomes_ a sorcerer. It involves a lot of delving in to occult secrets, a lot of personal cultivation, and a lot of hubris - it's not something that just happens by accident! I would have presumed the Immaculate order would have frowned on that whole process of attempting to become a magic man.<br /> <br /> Still, I suppose even if they frown on it, they're not going to start machine-gunning the training-grounds of the cabals of great Houses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/587-kukla","name":"Kukla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T01:41:46-07:00","id":1307179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Apromor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306133-mortal-sorcerers-in-the-realm?p=1307005#post1307005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bagrash Kol (sp?) was a mortal sorcerer who created an empire using the eye of autochthon in 1rst edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bagrash Kol was weird. In his first appearance as a previous user of the Eye of Autochthon in the 1e Storyteller's Companion there's no indication he was mortal. It makes a point of calling Ikerre unexalted but Kol is simply noted as a sorcerer. There's also this bit from Book of Three Circles-<br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/gCOT9Tt.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T02:38:19-07:00","id":1307182,"title":"","content":"This kind of conversation does make me wonder how much constraint there is on occult knowledge outside the Dragonblooded, and how much (if any) is needed before a person with the required talents can initiate into sorcery. <br /> <br /> Does the Realm's complex economy and government require a lot of drip down of occult knowledge into the general population, in the cities at least, whatever the Immaculate Philosophy might prefer? The peasant bulk probably do not have an easy time becoming sorcerers, though that's probably the case in every agrarian state in Creation (though controls on peasant movement maybe pose additional barriers in Realm).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T03:37:12-07:00","id":1307191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306133-mortal-sorcerers-in-the-realm?p=1307125#post1307125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess that makes sense! I suppose I'm mostly thinking about the process by which a mortal _becomes_ a sorcerer. It involves a lot of delving in to occult secrets, a lot of personal cultivation, and a lot of hubris - it's not something that just happens by accident!</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it kind of can, for certain initiations; the nightmare one, for instance. A character was still probably doing a thing, but the intent of that thing might not have been becoming a sorcerer, and in their ignorance they didn't realize that was where the path ended.<br /> <br /> I'll note that the Occult requirement is no higher than it is for the Exalted now. That's not saying that every mortal with Occult 3 can become a sorcerer, but for those who can, Occult 3 is a bit less onerous than Occult 5 was.<br /> <br /> Hmm, the initial sorcerers of Ysyr kind of became that by accident. A scenario I imagined was a peasant with the right potential stumbling accidentally into an uncapped demesne; not necessarily being mutated, but having a profound experience that opens their eyes a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T14:29:07-07:00","id":1307304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306133-mortal-sorcerers-in-the-realm?p=1307191#post1307191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll note that the Occult requirement is no higher than it is for the Exalted now. That's not saying that every mortal with Occult 3 can become a sorcerer, but for those who can, Occult 3 is a bit less onerous than Occult 5 was.</div> </div> </div> </div>Much less, and honestly, that does a lot to move things in to the 'It was kind of an accident' column, yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/587-kukla","name":"Kukla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T15:44:32-07:00","id":1307320,"title":"","content":"Hmm, looking at the description of Ability ratings, 3 is designated as skill above what might be expected of professional application, signifying experts or veterans.<br /> <br /> So I guess for peasants of the Realm, you still at least need somebody who has had a local role and a good amount of practical experience with the supernatural, but not necessarily access to formal training or extant knowledge. Conceivably somebody who has had to rack up a lot of time dealing with local spirits and the maladies they bring, because waiting for the proper authorities to get involved is not very efficient.<br /> <br /> Enough to get caught up in the orbit of some supernatural force, navigate some of the complicated interactions with it, and not back down when it's uncanny or threatening, but not exactly with a strict intent to become a sorcerer even though it effects that transformation in you.<br /> <br /> The Immaculate Order might not exactly punish you for having improper congress with such forces that can nonetheless now be put to the service of the Realm, but I imagine a space that produces a peasant sorcerer finds itself under stricter scrutiny for the next few years, as the monks chide the prefectural authorities for being lax in their duties.<br /> <br /> But supernatural phenomena pervades the world, such that it would be impractical either for a single organisation to handle all interactions with it or for many communities to get by without having local delegations of one kind of another to manage it. Per capita, the Blessed Isle might have the fewest such local delegates, but it has a lot of people.<br /> <br /> I would imagine that what few peasant sorcerers there are tend to come from the coastal islands, the mountains, and the deserts; places where life is a bit harsher and they probably need to deal with a lot of things on their own anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T20:36:37-07:00","id":1307396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306133-mortal-sorcerers-in-the-realm?p=1307125#post1307125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess that makes sense! I suppose I'm mostly thinking about the process by which a mortal _becomes_ a sorcerer. It involves a lot of delving in to occult secrets, a lot of personal cultivation, and a lot of hubris - it's not something that just happens by accident! I would have presumed the Immaculate order would have frowned on that whole process of attempting to become a magic man.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC, the Dev statement on what the Salinan Working means in 3e is that it transformed Creation such that if you have the potential to be a sorcerer, you <i>will</i> encounter opportunities to develop that potential. Assuming both that I recall that correctly and that it still holds, then there's a fundamental limit to how effective societal efforts to stop people from becoming sorcerers can be. After which you have to do <i>something</i> with the people who manage it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T00:03:15-07:00","id":1307426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306133-mortal-sorcerers-in-the-realm?p=1307396#post1307396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC, the Dev statement on what the Salinan Working means in 3e is that it transformed Creation such that if you have the potential to be a sorcerer, you <i>will</i> encounter opportunities to develop that potential.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't recall that, but I'm not certain the way <i>I</i> remember it is so solid, either*, so if you've got a cite for that, that'd be great.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ___________<br /> *In my recollection, the Salinan Working just preserves Sorcery via nature and a number of bound spirits; even if every textbook containing Death of Obsidian Butterflies were to suddenly burn up, and every sorcerer who knew the working of the spell died, you might intuit the spell from the migratory patterns of Southern butterflies and strange whisperings overheard between fire elementals, which even they do not understand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T08:07:20-07:00","id":1307477,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar572_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"572\" data-vbnamecard=\"572\">Verzio</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1226990#post1226990\">Never mind, found it:</a><br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When discussing the Salinan Working, it's necessary to distinguish between its First Edition and Second Edition presentations.<br /> <br /> In First Edition, the Salinan Working was a vast undertaking to preserve sorcerous knowledge, encoding the lessons needed to initiate into each circle of sorcery and a vast library of spells into Creation itself, leaving signs and clues in the patterns of the natural world that guide aspirants to spirits geased with sharing that information to those who ask in the appropriate way. In this manner, a great deal of sorcerous knowledge survived the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> In Second Edition, the Salinan Working, in addition to preserving sorcerous knowledge, also warped fate and causality such that any aspirant who desired to seek sorcery would inevitably come to encounter the five stations of initiation, and was but the first step to Salina's vision of making all circles of sorcery available to all sorcerers.<br /> <br /> In Ex3, we're going with the First Edition presentation of the Salinan Working.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T13:58:39-07:00","id":1307578,"title":"","content":"On a further tangent to the topic, this discussion makes more wonder what the Immaculate stance on the Salinan Working is, if they can tell that it exists. Some mysterious pattern in the world leading talented adepts towards sorcery - it seems like that could be played as either &quot;The work of the Immaculate Dragons!&quot; or &quot;Leftovers of anathema sorcery&quot;, and probably others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T14:15:10-07:00","id":1307584,"title":"","content":"I'll note that part of the First Edition description of the working is that you needed to actually know what you were looking for; the migration patterns of birds might have been made into something capable of teaching Travel Without Distance, but that didn't mean that every sorcerer who looked at migrating birds would immediately decode it.<br /> <br /> I think the part with getting spirit instruction was supposed to help a bit with this, but I feel as though the Salinan Working was not meant to read as a resounding success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T16:19:12-07:00","id":1307608,"title":"","content":"@TheCountAlucard<br /> <br /> Well, there's a reason I put in <i>two</i> caveats that I might be recalling incorrectly. Clearly my recall/phrasing was over-emphatic, too influenced by 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, my underlying point, which is that there's a limit to how much you can deny potential sorcerers access to knowledge, remains. You can socially discourage the pursuit, and certainly the Realm and IO will discourage mortals from doing so (with the level of pressure operating on a sliding scale depending on social class). But you'll still wind up with people learning sorcery anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}